1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,579
Three AI agents are at work.

2
00:00:02,629 --> 00:00:04,825
Who is actually in control?

3
00:00:05,575 --> 00:00:09,250
Three AI agents are running a
simulated company.

4
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:16,545
ReleaseOps ships releases, SupportOps works tickets
and refunds, InfraOps chases a cost spike.

5
00:00:16,595 --> 00:00:20,425
Every step they take is a
proposal, not an action.

6
00:00:21,175 --> 00:00:23,529
A production canary needs a human.

7
00:00:23,579 --> 00:00:28,761
The card shows the exact tool, the
parameters, the evidence, and the rule.

8
00:00:28,811 --> 00:00:32,650
Approve, and that consent is bound
to this action only.

9
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,892
Pause an agent, and its pending
approvals are revoked.

10
00:00:36,942 --> 00:00:39,975
Resume, and it re-plans from
the current state.

11
00:00:40,725 --> 00:00:46,969
Now a poisoned runbook tells InfraOps to export
the customer table to an outside bucket.

12
00:00:47,019 --> 00:00:51,618
Policy blocks it before any effect, and
the agent is quarantined.

13
00:00:51,668 --> 00:00:55,624
Without the tower, twelve thousand
rows would have left.

14
00:00:55,674 --> 00:00:56,625
With it, zero.

15
00:00:57,375 --> 00:00:57,908
Kill it.

16
00:00:57,958 --> 00:01:05,050
Its epoch is fenced, so when a stale worker retries the
cached export, the commit gate refuses it.

17
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:14,183
Replay shows the last steps from the persisted log: what it
proposed, what policy said, what it cost, and who intervened.

18
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:19,550
The audit export is scoped to your team, and
its hash chain verifies offline.

19
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:21,056
WATCHSHIFT.

20
00:01:21,106 --> 00:01:23,179
The agent can think anything.

21
00:01:23,229 --> 00:01:26,475
It can only do what the control plane allows.
